ronous Optical Network (SONET) based ethernet, legacy data hosting services, and conferencing services; and managed and professional service solutions, as well as sells communications equipment. The company also provides high speed and lower speed broadband service to residential and small business customers; local and long-distance voice services, professional services, and other ancillary services; and federal broadband and state support programs. It serves its products and services under the Lumen, CenturyLink, Black Lotus Labs, and Quantum Fiber brand name. The company was formerly known as CenturyLink, Inc. and changed its name to Lumen Technologies, Inc. in September 2020. Lumen Technologies, Inc. was incorporated in 1968 and is headquartered in Monroe, Louisiana.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Kathleen E. Johnson | CEO & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $6.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 24K people. Revenue per employee of $517K ranks in the below the sector median among Communication Services peers. Each employee generates $15K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 12\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Lumen Technologies, Inc. is a mid-cap communication services business with a $4.2B market cap on $12.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -11% over the past three years and -4% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 0% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $371M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 8.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -0.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 10.0% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Communication Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.4pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 15% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 86/100): structural revenue/margin decline; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Communication Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 78% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 21% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Insiders are net buyers (75% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $0.8M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is Lumen (NYSE:LUMN) Betting on AI Fiber?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/penny/is-lumen-nyselumn-betting-on-ai-fiber","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794403020.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.128,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Lumen Technologies (NYSE:LUMN) Stock: Insider Michelle Goldberg Buys 25,000 Shares","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/lumen-technologies-nyselumn-stock-insider-michelle-goldberg-buys-25000-shares.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794391875.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.878,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Lumen Technologies (NYSE:LUMN) CEO Kathleen Johnson Purchases 100,000 Shares of Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/lumen-technologies-nyselumn-ceo-kathleen-johnson-purchases-100000-shares-of-stock.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794302598.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.836,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["leadership"]},{"title":"Lumen Technologies (LUMN) Stock May Trade Below Fair Value On AI Network Launch","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/telecom/nasdaq-lumn/lumen-technologies/news/lumen-technologies-lumn-stock-may-trade-below-fair-value-on","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794238131.877,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.944,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["product"]},{"title":"Lumen Technologies Director Michelle J. Goldberg Acquires 25,000 Shares at $3.91 Each","source":"kalkineme